<UserControl
    x:Class="MCPRouter.Shell.Views.SettingsBoard"
    xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
    xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
    xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
    xmlns:automation="using:Microsoft.UI.Xaml.Automation"
    mc:Ignorable="d">

    <!--
      SEVEN SECTIONS, AND EVERY ONE OF THEM ADDRESSABLE. DEF-076: this board declared three
      sections against a WIN13 ledger row claiming seven, and its three ToggleSwitches carried no
      accessible name at all - so the out-of-process UIA read of the live board found `Copy` and
      nothing else actuable, and reported "not one ToggleSwitch". Both halves of that were true
      and neither was the whole story: a WinUI ToggleSwitch publishes as a Button carrying
      TogglePattern, so the three were in the tree as three anonymous Buttons.

      Two things follow, and they are why this file looks the way it does.

      NAMES ARE NOT DECORATION HERE. A control with no accessible name cannot be asserted against
      by name, so every case on this surface would stand at `presence`; the same tree serves
      Narrator, so it is an accessibility defect and a measurability defect in one. Every section
      container and every toggle carries an AutomationProperties.Name.

      IDS, NOT NAMES, ARE WHAT THE LANE ADDRESSES. A UIA name search returns the first element
      carrying that name anywhere in the tree, and this shell's menu bar already holds a "Router"
      and a "Help". So each section and each toggle also carries an AutomationProperties.AutomationId
      from SettingsPresentation - the view and the lane read the same source for them, rather than
      both retyping the string.

      AND THE TOGGLES ARE BOUND. `IsOn="True"` on an unbound switch is the inert-UI failure one
      layer along: it flips and nothing happens. Each one now writes through
      SettingsBoardModel.UpdateToggle, and the readout at the foot re-renders from the model's
      state - so flipping a switch changes something OUTSIDE the switch that was flipped, which
      is the only difference an out-of-process reader can see between a live control and a dead one.
    -->
    <Grid x:Name="RootGrid" Background="Transparent">
        <ScrollViewer VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto">
            <StackPanel Padding="24,16,24,32" Spacing="20" MaxWidth="800" HorizontalAlignment="Left">

                <TextBlock Text="Settings" Style="{ThemeResource TitleTextBlockStyle}" FontWeight="SemiBold" />

                <!-- 1. Router -->
                <TextBlock Text="Router" Style="{ThemeResource SubtitleTextBlockStyle}" FontWeight="SemiBold" />
                <Border x:Name="RouterSection"
                        automation:AutomationProperties.Name="Router"
                        automation:AutomationProperties.AutomationId="settings.section.router"
                        automation:AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Control"
                        Background="{ThemeResource CardBackgroundFillColorDefaultBrush}"
                        BorderBrush="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultBrush}"
                        BorderThickness="1"
                        CornerRadius="{ThemeResource ControlCornerRadius}"
                        Padding="16,12">
                    <StackPanel Spacing="12">
                        <Grid>
                            <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                <ColumnDefinition Width="*" />
                                <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
                            </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                            <StackPanel>
                                <TextBlock Text="Loopback Endpoint" FontWeight="SemiBold" />
                                <TextBlock x:Name="EndpointText" Style="{ThemeResource CaptionTextBlockStyle}" Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}" />
                            </StackPanel>
                            <Button Grid.Column="1"
                                    Content="Copy"
                                    automation:AutomationProperties.Name="Copy the loopback endpoint"
                                    automation:AutomationProperties.AutomationId="settings.action.copyEndpoint"
                                    VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                        </Grid>

                        <Grid>
                            <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                <ColumnDefinition Width="*" />
                                <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
                            </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                            <StackPanel>
                                <TextBlock Text="Launch router daemon at sign-in" FontWeight="SemiBold" />
                                <TextBlock Text="Starts the background loopback service automatically." Style="{ThemeResource CaptionTextBlockStyle}" Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}" />
                            </StackPanel>
                            <ToggleSwitch x:Name="LaunchAtLoginToggle"
                                          Grid.Column="1"
                                          Tag="LaunchAtLogin"
                                          Toggled="OnToggled"
                                          VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                        </Grid>
                    </StackPanel>
                </Border>

                <!-- 2. Harnesses - governance, not configuration. -->
                <TextBlock Text="Harnesses" Style="{ThemeResource SubtitleTextBlockStyle}" FontWeight="SemiBold" />
                <Border x:Name="HarnessesSection"
                        automation:AutomationProperties.Name="Harnesses"
                        automation:AutomationProperties.AutomationId="settings.section.harnesses"
                        automation:AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Control"
                        Background="{ThemeResource CardBackgroundFillColorDefaultBrush}"
                        BorderBrush="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultBrush}"
                        BorderThickness="1"
                        CornerRadius="{ThemeResource ControlCornerRadius}"
                        Padding="16,12">
                    <TextBlock x:Name="HarnessesGovernanceText"
                               Style="{ThemeResource BodyTextBlockStyle}"
                               Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"
                               TextWrapping="Wrap" />
                </Border>

                <!-- 3. Session analyst -->
                <TextBlock Text="Session analyst" Style="{ThemeResource SubtitleTextBlockStyle}" FontWeight="SemiBold" />
                <Border x:Name="SessionAnalystSection"
                        automation:AutomationProperties.Name="Session analyst"
                        automation:AutomationProperties.AutomationId="settings.section.sessionanalyst"
                        automation:AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Control"
                        Background="{ThemeResource CardBackgroundFillColorDefaultBrush}"
                        BorderBrush="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultBrush}"
                        BorderThickness="1"
                        CornerRadius="{ThemeResource ControlCornerRadius}"
                        Padding="16,12">
                    <TextBlock x:Name="AnalystGovernanceText"
                               Style="{ThemeResource BodyTextBlockStyle}"
                               Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"
                               TextWrapping="Wrap" />
                </Border>

                <!-- 4. Updates -->
                <TextBlock Text="Updates" Style="{ThemeResource SubtitleTextBlockStyle}" FontWeight="SemiBold" />
                <Border x:Name="UpdatesSection"
                        automation:AutomationProperties.Name="Updates"
                        automation:AutomationProperties.AutomationId="settings.section.updates"
                        automation:AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Control"
                        Background="{ThemeResource CardBackgroundFillColorDefaultBrush}"
                        BorderBrush="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultBrush}"
                        BorderThickness="1"
                        CornerRadius="{ThemeResource ControlCornerRadius}"
                        Padding="16,12">
                    <TextBlock x:Name="UpdatesGovernanceText"
                               Style="{ThemeResource BodyTextBlockStyle}"
                               Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"
                               TextWrapping="Wrap" />
                </Border>

                <!-- 5. Security -->
                <TextBlock Text="Security &amp; Confirmations" Style="{ThemeResource SubtitleTextBlockStyle}" FontWeight="SemiBold" />
                <Border x:Name="SecuritySection"
                        automation:AutomationProperties.Name="Security"
                        automation:AutomationProperties.AutomationId="settings.section.security"
                        automation:AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Control"
                        Background="{ThemeResource CardBackgroundFillColorDefaultBrush}"
                        BorderBrush="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultBrush}"
                        BorderThickness="1"
                        CornerRadius="{ThemeResource ControlCornerRadius}"
                        Padding="16,12">
                    <Grid>
                        <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="*" />
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
                        </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <StackPanel>
                            <TextBlock Text="Require confirmation on destructive operations" FontWeight="SemiBold" />
                            <TextBlock Text="Prompts before removing servers, skills, or deleting stored tokens." Style="{ThemeResource CaptionTextBlockStyle}" Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}" />
                        </StackPanel>
                        <ToggleSwitch x:Name="RequireConfirmationToggle"
                                      Grid.Column="1"
                                      Tag="RequireConfirmationOnDestructive"
                                      Toggled="OnToggled"
                                      VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                    </Grid>
                </Border>

                <!-- 6. Ambient surface -->
                <TextBlock Text="Ambient Notification Surface" Style="{ThemeResource SubtitleTextBlockStyle}" FontWeight="SemiBold" />
                <Border x:Name="AmbientSurfaceSection"
                        automation:AutomationProperties.Name="Ambient surface"
                        automation:AutomationProperties.AutomationId="settings.section.ambientsurface"
                        automation:AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Control"
                        Background="{ThemeResource CardBackgroundFillColorDefaultBrush}"
                        BorderBrush="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultBrush}"
                        BorderThickness="1"
                        CornerRadius="{ThemeResource ControlCornerRadius}"
                        Padding="16,12">
                    <Grid>
                        <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="*" />
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
                        </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <StackPanel>
                            <TextBlock Text="Show status in notification area" FontWeight="SemiBold" />
                            <TextBlock Text="Displays ambient router status and queued inbox items in the Windows tray." Style="{ThemeResource CaptionTextBlockStyle}" Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}" />
                        </StackPanel>
                        <ToggleSwitch x:Name="ShowAmbientIconToggle"
                                      Grid.Column="1"
                                      Tag="ShowAmbientIcon"
                                      Toggled="OnToggled"
                                      VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                    </Grid>
                </Border>

                <!-- 7. Advanced - the router's own facts, and the live readout of the three toggles. -->
                <TextBlock Text="Advanced" Style="{ThemeResource SubtitleTextBlockStyle}" FontWeight="SemiBold" />
                <Border x:Name="AdvancedSection"
                        automation:AutomationProperties.Name="Advanced"
                        automation:AutomationProperties.AutomationId="settings.section.advanced"
                        automation:AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Control"
                        Background="{ThemeResource CardBackgroundFillColorDefaultBrush}"
                        BorderBrush="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultBrush}"
                        BorderThickness="1"
                        CornerRadius="{ThemeResource ControlCornerRadius}"
                        Padding="16,12">
                    <StackPanel Spacing="8">
                        <StackPanel>
                            <TextBlock Text="Router home" FontWeight="SemiBold" />
                            <TextBlock x:Name="HomeDirectoryText" Style="{ThemeResource CaptionTextBlockStyle}" Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}" TextWrapping="Wrap" />
                        </StackPanel>
                        <StackPanel>
                            <TextBlock Text="Idle reaper" FontWeight="SemiBold" />
                            <TextBlock x:Name="IdleReaperText" Style="{ThemeResource CaptionTextBlockStyle}" Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}" />
                        </StackPanel>
                        <TextBlock x:Name="FilesHelpText"
                                   Style="{ThemeResource CaptionTextBlockStyle}"
                                   Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"
                                   TextWrapping="Wrap" />
                        <!-- The readout DEF-076's fix is proved by. Its text is rendered from the
                             model, never from the switches, so a switch that fails to write
                             through leaves it unmoved. -->
                        <!-- No AutomationProperties.Name here, deliberately. A TextBlock
                             publishes its own Text as its accessible name; a static Name would
                             override it, and the readout would then report the same string
                             forever however the model moved. The first census run measured
                             exactly that and called the board inert. Addressing is the
                             AutomationId's job; the name is the value. -->
                        <TextBlock x:Name="StateSummaryText"
                                   automation:AutomationProperties.AutomationId="settings.state.summary"
                                   Style="{ThemeResource CaptionTextBlockStyle}"
                                   FontFamily="Consolas"
                                   Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"
                                   TextWrapping="Wrap" />
                    </StackPanel>
                </Border>
            </StackPanel>
        </ScrollViewer>
    </Grid>
</UserControl>
